 ### Question
 
 What default retention applies to raw media in an explicitly enabled continuous or near-continuous perception session?
 
 ### Current direction
 
-Delta §17.8. Minimize retained raw surveillance under DESIGN.md §12.2. Decide transient buffers, purposeful clips, local storage eligibility and expiry, without confusing deletion of media with editing append-only historical evidence. Do not promise automated retention enforcement before implementation.
+Delta §17.8. `UBU-D0327` specifies zero durable raw retention by default, a memory-only buffer capped at 60 seconds from acquisition, and explicitly approved purpose-scoped clips on eligible encrypted local storage with a 24-hour default expiry from the earliest captured sample. DESIGN.md §12.2 separates access expiry, pending/completed cleanup and append-only historical evidence. Automated enforcement remains an implementation gate, not a shipped claim.
 
 ### Resolution
 
-Open.
+Resolved by `UBU-D0327`: DESIGN.md §12.2 defines transient raw-buffer age and resource limits, interruption cleanup, explicit clip-retention approval, local storage eligibility and absolute expiry. Review, retries, copies and restart cannot renew deadlines; longer finite clip retention requires separate approval before expiry. Raw deletion preserves only permitted append-only claim/correction/deletion metadata, and minimized derivatives need their own policy authority. Revision-pinned retention and failure checks are required before enablement; this resolves the policy contract, not implementation or physical erasure. `UBU-Q0171`, `UBU-Q0168`, `UBU-Q0177` and `UBU-Q0162` retain operator-control, measured-performance, hardware and Log-enforcement scope.
 
